            <ArticleTitle>[Acute appendicitis: the benefit of a wait-and-see attitude].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>203-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute appendicitis. Acute appendicitis is often suspected but in 70% of the cases the complaints to an other diagnosis. Aggressive therapy is therefore not indicated. A 12 to 24 h observation allows to avoid surgery and complications which are not exceptional.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
